quran[12]{c,v,t}:
  20,65,"They (the magicians) said: ‘O Musa (Moses)! Either you should throw (first), or we shall be the first to throw.’"
  20,66,"He (Moses) said: ‘Rather you throw (first).’ Then, behold, their ropes and sticks appeared to him by their magic (as though) they were moving around fast."
  20,67,So Musa (Moses) concealed the alarm he felt in his mind.
  20,68,"We said: ‘Do not worry. Indeed, you will have the upper hand."
  20,69,Throw down what is in your right hand. It will swallow up whatever they have produced. What they have produced is only a magician’s trick. And the magician will not be successful wherever he may come.’
  20,70,"Then, the magicians were cast down in prostration. They said: ‘We believe in the Lord of Harun (Aaron) and Musa (Moses).’"
  20,71,He (Pharaoh) said: ‘Do you profess faith in him before I permit you? He is indeed your chief who has taught you magic! I shall surely cut off your hands and your feet from opposite sides. And I shall surely crucify you on the trunks of palm trees. So you shall surely know which of us is more severe and more lasting in punishing.’
  20,72,"They (the magicians) said: ‘We will never prefer you over the clear proofs that have come to us, nor over Him Who has created us. So decide whatever you (are determined to) decide. You can only decide about the life of this world."
  20,73,"Indeed, we have believed in our Lord so He may forgive us our sins and that magic you compelled us to perform. And Allah is the Best and the Everlasting.’"
  20,74,"Whoever comes to his Lord as an evildoer will certainly have Hell, where he will neither die nor live."
  20,75,"But whoever comes to Him as a believer, having performed righteous deeds, for such shall be the highest ranks (in Paradise),"
  20,76,the Gardens of Eternity with rivers flowing beneath them. They will abide in them forever. And that is the reward of the one who purifies (himself).
